            "review_title": "Review at Bờ Kè Mr. Crab",
            "review_text": "1926yanks\nSeattle, Washington755 contributions\n0\nSimply Outstanding\nMar 2025 • Friends\nI’m often surprised that spectacular restaurant like this has so few reviews on TA. Then I realize most tourists are not exploring & brave enough to go to fabulous, authentic places that locals eat at. \nProb 90% of people who eat here are from VN. It does not look touristy. 90% of tourists eat in pseudo-authentic places. And they pay 2x or 3x of what they pay at places like this. \nThe shrimp salad was great-so tasty, big, & a little spicy. $6US. We had 3 large crabs (totaling 1.5 lbs, .68 kilo) for less than $40: one grilled with garlic, another with salted egg sauce with corn kernels, & the third with tamarind sauce. \nYou literally go to the dozens of tubs with running water & pick your meal. It is weighed right there. That is almost worth “the price of admission.”\nOk, the napkins are paper and small (there is a bank of sinks with soap in the restaurant where you wash your sticky hands. It is sad how many tourists play it “safe” and miss out on culinary delights & experiences & pay 2x or 3x in the process.\nRead more\nWritten March 13, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
